-- 3. Scaling test -- the decisive check ---------------------
   A real bias stays put as the sample grows; noise shrinks as
   1/sqrt(n). We remeasure each candidate at n, 10n and 100n on
   fresh seeds and look at how the value moves. This separates a
   genuine characteristic from the maximum of 9216 noisy estimates,
   which a single rerun cannot do.
